                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1278-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Milab Microphones SRND 360</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Milab SRND 360 is a compact 6-channel surround microphone. By combining signals from the 3 matched DC196 rectangular condenser capsules, an additional 3 cardioid &#8220;virtual&#8221; capsules can be accessed. The three physical cardioid capsules are spaced 120&deg; apart.</p><p><a href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/milab/SRND-PSU-rear.jpg" rel="shadowbox"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/milab/SRND-PSU-rear-sm.jpg" width="200" alt="Milab SRND 360 power supply/breakout box" class="thumb shaft" /></a>A single multipin XLR cable connects the microphone to its power supply box. The rear of the PSU provides six discrete mono XLR outputs, marked left/center/right, front/rear as follows: LF, CF, RF, LR, CR, RR.</p><p>The SRND 360 can also be used as a single cardioid front facing or XY stereo rear facing by selecting the appropriate outputs on the power supply box.</p><blockquote><p><cite>Resolution 2009</cite><br />The SRND 360 proved fabulous at generating rock-solid imaging when played back in 5.1, and in the case of the drum kit, again very little in terms of smearing of transient sounds. Where it wasn&#8217;t quite as good was in capturing a useful surround ambiance in the rears&#8230;I guess that&#8217;s the trade-off between a compact coincident array and a spaced mic technique for surround work.</p></blockquote><p><a href="http://blog.mixonline.com/briefingroom/2010/12/15/rycote-to-design-custom-shock-mounts-for-milab-microphones/">Milab and Rycote partnered</a> to develop a custom version of the inVision shockmount compatible with the large diameter SRND 360.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Milab/SRND-360">Milab Microphones SRND-360</a></p>
